  "description": "QAKJAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C190 H260 Cl2 N8 Nd10 O76 P4 S16,3(C3 H7 N1 O1),7(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd9 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd10 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.689-4.148 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.74-118.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd10(BSC4A)4(MePO3)4(Cl)2(OH)4(H2O)4(DMF)8(MeOH)]·3DMF·7CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
